# Sample calls for the Card Control API (Visual Studio, VS Code REST Client, Rider).
#
# Before you start:
#   1. Run the identity provider (5090), tokenisation stub (5070), card platform stub (5080) and this API (5190).
#   2. Encrypt a PAN from the repository root and paste the output as the encryptedPan value on line 4, on one line:
#        dotnet run tools/jwe-tool.cs -- encrypt --key .dev-keys/bank-dev-1.public.pem 4111111111111111
#   3. Send the access token request (the first request below) first. The other requests reuse it.
#
# Seed cards: 4111111111111111 CORP-1001 Active, 4242424242424242 CORP-1001 Locked,
#             4012888888881881 CORP-2002 Active, 4000056655665556 CORP-2002 Cancelled,
#             4000002500003155 CORP-3003 Active, 4000000000003220 no corporate, Active.
# The partner is enabled for CORP-1001 and CORP-2002 only.

###
# Get a partner access token (client credentials). Send this first.
# @name partnerToken
POST {{idp}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=partner-app&client_secret=dev-only-partner-app-secret&scope=api%3A%2F%2Fcard-control%2F.default

### Lock the card. Expect 200, status Locked
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Lock it again. Expect 409 CardAlreadyLocked
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Unlock the card. Expect 200, status Active
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/unlock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Corporate the partner is not enabled for. Expect 403 CorporateNotEnabled
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-3003"
}

### Card named with the wrong corporate. Expect 404 CardNotFound
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-2002"
}

### No X-Initiating-User header. Expect 400 InvalidRequest
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Clear PAN instead of a JWE. Expect 400 InvalidEncryptedPan
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "4111111111111111",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### No token. Expect 401
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

###
# Get a token without the CardControl.Write role (partner-readonly).
# @name readonlyToken
POST {{idp}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=partner-readonly&client_secret=dev-only-partner-readonly-secret&scope=api%3A%2F%2Fcard-control%2F.default

### Use that token. Expect 403
POST {{api}}/v1/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{readonlyToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Card platform audit trail for the 4111 card (stub admin API)
GET {{cards}}/cards/ctok_8f3a1c2e9b7d4a01/audit

### Make the card platform flaky, 30 percent of calls fail
PUT {{cards}}/admin/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 0, "errorRate": 0.3 }

### Make the card platform slow, 3 seconds per call. Lock then returns 504
PUT {{cards}}/admin/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 3000, "errorRate": 0 }

### Reset the card platform (seed data, faults and audit trail)
POST {{cards}}/admin/reset

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{api}}/healthz

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
